  "body": "https://whatpr.org/html/3934/rendering.html#the-fieldset-and-legend-elements\r\n\r\nUAs disagree on how to handle this [testcase](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=6140).\r\n\r\nFirefox creates list item markers, but the item numbers are zero.  Also, if you add `border-width:100px` it places the markers on top of the border so I'm guessing it creates markers for its inner anonymous block box rather than the outer fieldset box.\r\n\r\nEdge gets the numbers right but places the marker above the fieldset when there's a rendered legend, which seems wrong.\r\n\r\nChrome doesn't create any markers at all.\r\n\r\nSafari seems to handle the testcase correctly (assuming we want to support list-item fieldsets).\r\n\r\nCurrently the spec says that `display:list-item` behaves as `block` and thus that Chrome has the correct layout, but I wonder if that's really what we want.  It seems to me that supporting `display:list-item` would be more useful to authors.",
